<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-19723] TCU: Tolerate ENOSPC failure when moving files into Trash Can</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19723</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When unlink a file under TCU enabled, it may fail with ENOSPC as the inodes space is used out for TCU insert/create pFID operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this case, the simple solution is that MDT tolerates the ENOSPC error,  just treat as TCU is disabled and bypass TCU and destroy the file directly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The much complex solution is that for a removing directory, we append the full path (like fid2path) into "trusted.unrm" XATTR to the pFID stub file in Trash Can to avoid the "pFID" stub file becoming a orphan object.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
